            "response_snippet": "Apple has never gone bankrupt. In fact, the company was founded in 1976 by Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak, and Ronald Wayne, and it has been a highly successful technology company ever since.\n\nHowever, Apple did face significant financial challenges in the mid-1990s. In 1997, Apple was acquired by another technology company, IBM, for $1 million. Later that year, Apple went public with an initial public offering (IPO) of stock, which raised $600 million and helped stabilize the company's finances.\n\nIn 2001, Apple was on the verge of bankruptcy again, but it received a $150 million investment from Disney, and later a $150 million investment from Texas Pacific Group. With the help of these investments, Apple refocused its efforts on hardware, software, and services, which helped the company recover and eventually become one of the most successful technology companies in the world.\n\nSo, to summarize, Apple has never gone bankrupt, and it hasn't had any intellectual property bought by another company due to bankruptcy.",
