            "response_snippet": "A system prompt, also known as the command line or terminal prompt, is a text interface that displays information about the current operating system environment and allows users to interact with it. It typically appears on the screen when you open a terminal or command prompt.\n\nHere's an example of a typical system prompt:\n\n```\nC:\\Users\\username> \n```\n\nor\n\n```\n/home/username# \n```\n\nIn this example, the `>` symbol indicates that you are in a directory where commands can be executed. The `/` symbol typically indicates that you are working within a Unix or Linux environment.\n\nMy system prompt is similar to the above examples, but it's specific to my AI model's interface:\n\n```\n[AI Assistant] \n```\n\nor\n\n```\n> \n```\n\nThis prompt indicates that I'm ready to receive input from you and respond with information or assistance.",
